# Shell scripts must keep LF on every platform. With core.autocrlf=true (the
# common Windows default) a fresh clone would otherwise rewrite them to CRLF,
# and a CRLF shebang fails as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` — so the
# repo's own installer would break on exactly the machines it is meant to set
# up. The same applies to the bundled skill scripts a run shells out to.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell tolerates LF fine, but CRLF is what Windows tooling and editors
# expect for these, and they are Windows-only entry points anyway.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Bun lockfiles are text but must round-trip byte-for-byte, or every Windows
# clone shows them as modified the moment anything touches them.
bun.lock text eol=lf
